Metadata-Version: 2.1
Name: pywin32
Version: 306
Summary: Minimal ctypes stand-in for pywin32, supplying only what Deluge calls.
Author: Deluge ARM64 bundle
License: Same terms as the surrounding bundle
Platform: win32

This is NOT the real pywin32.

MSYS2/MinGW CPython cannot load pywin32's binary extensions - they are built
against the MSVC CPython ABI - and no win_arm64 wheel exists for this
interpreter either. Deluge imports six pywin32 modules on Windows, and every
call it makes is a thin wrapper over a documented Win32 API, so those calls are
reimplemented with ctypes instead:

  win32api      SetConsoleCtrlHandler, GetFileAttributes, GetLastError,
                CloseHandle
  win32con      CTRL_*_EVENT and FILE_ATTRIBUTE_* constants
  win32event    CreateMutex
  win32file     GetDiskFreeSpaceEx
  win32process  EnumProcesses
  winerror      ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS and friends

This distribution exists so that pkg_resources can satisfy Deluge's declared
"pywin32; sys_platform == win32" requirement, which it resolves when loading UI
entry points and when activating plugin eggs. Anything beyond the names listed
above is absent - do not treat this as a general pywin32 replacement.
